---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data';
---
<Base
  title="Telkomsel Orbit, Glen Hutajulu"
  description="A website revamp for a fixed wireless internet service."
>
<article>
<section class="cs-hero" aria-label="Telkomsel Orbit">
<p class="cs-kick mono"><span class="sq" style="color: var(--acc)"></span>Case study &#123;03&#125; · Telkomsel Orbit · Telco, 2024</p>
<h1 class="cs-name px-font intro" aria-label="Telkomsel Orbit"><span aria-hidden="true"><span class="c" style="--i: 0">o</span><span class="c" style="--i: 1">r</span><span class="c" style="--i: 2">b</span><span class="c" style="--i: 3">i</span><span class="c" style="--i: 4">t</span></span></h1>
<div class="cs-sub">
<p class="lede">A website revamp for a fixed wireless internet service.</p>
<a class="pill mono" href="#story">Read the story ↓</a>
</div>
</section>

<div class="cs-cover"><div class="cs-cover-in"><img src="/work/orbit/cover.webp" width="2400" height="1280" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" alt="Telkomsel Orbit website on a laptop beside two phones"></div></div>
<section class="cs-sum" id="story" aria-label="Project summary">
<dl>
<div class="rv"><dt class="mono">Problem</dt><dd>Orbit needed a clearer website structure and simpler login, purchase and modem pairing flows to support its expanding digital ecosystem.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.08s"><dt class="mono">Role and team</dt><dd>UI/UX Designer at Aleph, working in a project team.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.16s"><dt class="mono">Outcome</dt><dd>Partially released between June and December 2024. The client did not share post-launch metrics.</dd></div>
<div class="rv" style="--d: 0.24s"><dt class="mono">Timeline</dt><dd>Mar 2024 – Nov 2024</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Overview">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;00&#125;</b>Overview</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<p class="rv">Telkomsel Orbit is a fixed wireless internet service under Telkomsel. It set out on a major website revamp to improve the user experience and support its expanding digital ecosystem. I joined as a UI/UX Designer and supported the work across multiple touchpoints, from structural layout to system integration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Navigation">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;01&#125;</b>Navigation</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">a clearer way through the website</h2>
<p class="rv">I ran heuristic evaluations and user testing to simplify navigation and improve the content hierarchy across the Orbit website.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Content">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;02&#125;</b>Content</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">content people can follow</h2>
<p class="rv">I revamped copy and visual structure for better readability, engagement and product clarity across key pages, including Home, Product and Support.</p>
</div>
</section>
<div class="trio">
<figure class="rv"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/orbit/web-home.webp" width="1440" height="4884" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Telkomsel Orbit homepage with promotions, shortcuts and modem options"></div><figcaption class="mono">Homepage · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.1s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/orbit/web-modem.webp" width="1440" height="3010" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Modem product page with package options, specifications and features"></div><figcaption class="mono">Modem product page · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: 0.2s"><div class="shot"><img src="/work/orbit/web-halo.webp" width="1440" height="6226" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Halo Orbit program page with benefits, packages and activation guide"></div><figcaption class="mono">Halo Orbit program page · Hover to scroll</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Activation">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;03&#125;</b>Activation</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">getting a modem up and running</h2>
<p class="rv">Working closely with the tech team, I redesigned and optimised the journeys for login, customer purchase and modem pairing via the website, to simplify onboarding for new users.</p>
<p class="rv">Activation could start from a QR scan or a purchase email, with or without creating an account. Each path also covers what can go wrong: a modem that is not connected, an invalid field, a wrong OTP or a KTP that fails.</p>
</div>
</section>
<div class="pair" style="grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 347fr) minmax(0, 244fr)">
<figure class="rv"><div class="panel"><img src="/work/orbit/flow-entry.webp" width="1800" height="1038" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Flow map of activation entry points, including QR scan, purchase email and activation without an account"></div><figcaption class="mono">Activation entry points</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="rv" style="--d: .1s"><div class="panel"><img src="/work/orbit/flow-prepaid.webp" width="1788" height="1464" decoding="async" loading="lazy" alt="Flow map of prepaid activation on the web with its error states"></div><figcaption class="mono">Prepaid activation and its error states</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Ecosystem">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;04&#125;</b>Ecosystem</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">one experience with mytelkomsel</h2>
<p class="rv">With the product owners, I worked on a seamless cross-platform experience between the Orbit website and app and the MyTelkomsel app, particularly for account syncing and modem status visibility.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ch" aria-label="Status">
<p class="ch-n mono"><b>&#123;05&#125;</b>Status</p>
<div class="ch-body">
<h2 class="px-font rv">where it stands</h2>
<p class="rv">The revamp was partially released between June and December 2024. The client did not share post-launch metrics, so I have no numbers to show. Internal feedback noted better synergy between Orbit's web platform and Telkomsel's broader digital ecosystem.</p>
</div>
</section>
<nav class="next" aria-label="Next case study">
<p class="mono">Next case study &#123;04&#125;</p>
<a class="px-font" href="/work/byu">byU <span>↗</span></a>
<p class="mono"><a href="/#work" style="font-size: 12px; display: inline; color: #0E0F11; text-decoration: underline">Back to all work</a></p>
</nav>
</article>
</Base>
